rtLine":176,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":177,"endLineOffset":45,"length":81}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7390,"endPos":7432,"startLine":216,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":216,"endLineOffset":57,"length":43},{"pos":7448,"endPos":7490,"startLine":217,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":217,"endLineOffset":57,"length":43},{"pos":7506,"endPos":7566,"startLine":218,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":218,"endLineOffset":75,"length":61}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/EsRelation.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/EsRelation.java-1463:1491-","promptId":"#SCJ3S","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/EsRelation.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/EsRelation.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1463,"endPos":1491,"startLine":38,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":38,"endLineOffset":32,"length":29}],"dstChanges":[]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":129,"line":129,"comment_lines":["[][129]"],"review_comment":["Why is this map needed?","It is used in LocalExecutionPlanner:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/2ff1d769a61a6c4974b4ab3347ec668d5abf0da4/x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/planner/LocalExecutionPlanner.java#L564-L571","If this is the only thing that requires that: I believe this check could happen much earlier. Potentially already in the analyzer on the coordinator node. We shouldn\u0027t need to wait until the local planning to determine that an index isn\u0027t a lookup index.\r\n\r\nCould you maybe check if it\u0027s feasible to move that to an earlier place and, thus, remove the `indexNameWithModes` map altogether from the `EsRelation` and related classes?\r\n\r\nHappy to assist with moving that to an earlier stage!","There already is an index mode check in the Analyzer: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/4ac8d55ff7c5612413e4a45e14a2b39f3e85f3a9/x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java#L239-L255","I think I got it. The check is indeed already performed and could be removed - it\u0027s just there out of defensiveness as far as I can see.\r\n\r\nWhat cannot be removed is the line\r\n```\r\n var entry \u003d indicesWithModes.entrySet().iterator().next(); \r\n```\r\nwhich, in case of aliases, contains the _actual_ lookup index name in the entry\u0027s key.\r\n\r\nLooks to me like we should add a comment and leave this as-is. (Well, and maybe remove the defensive double validation, but it also doesn\u0027t hurt.)\r\n\r\nI\u0027ll confirm with @idegtiarenko if this is what we want to do.","Correct. IndexName could actually be alias or pattern, while map entries include resolved index names","@costin , we decided removing this map is too large in scope for this PR. Ievgen opened a follow-up issue: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/120210","The map seems similar to EsIndex - it\u0027s detailed information that isn\u0027t required.\r\nNit: doing it in a separate PR will require a transport bump; maybe consider this complete but not merge, do the follow-up PR and then merge them at the same time to have only one increment?","I am not sure I would be able to pick up followup immediately.\r\nAlso keeping this updated required multiple conflict resolutions. \r\nI would really prefer to merge this earlier."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/EsQueryExec.java","id":36263,"created_at":"2025-01-08T06:23:44Z","original_position":46,"side":"RIGHT","position":51,"submitted_on_commit":"611ccae740ee25c64bfab1ca6b263be30c7c329d","diff_hunk":"@@ -108,23 +111,32 @@ public FieldAttribute field() {\n         }\n     }\n \n-    public EsQueryExec(Source source, EsIndex index, IndexMode indexMode, List\u003cAttribute\u003e attributes, QueryBuilder query) {\n-        this(source, index, indexMode, attributes, query, null, null, null);\n+    public EsQueryExec(\n+        Source source,\n+        String indexName,\n+        IndexMode indexMode,\n+        Map\u003cString, IndexMode\u003e indexNameWithModes,\n+        List\u003cAttribute\u003e attributes,\n+        QueryBuilder query\n+    ) {\n+        this(source, indexName, indexMode, indexNameWithModes, attributes, query, null, null, null);\n     }\n \n     public EsQueryExec(\n         Source source,\n-        EsIndex index,\n+        String indexName,\n         IndexMode indexMode,\n+        Map\u003cString, IndexMode\u003e indexNameWithModes,","submitted_line":129},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":129,"line":129,"comment_lines":["[129][]"],"review_comment":["This test file beautifully demonstrates the improvements from the change. Awesome, in this particularly bad case we got a reduction by 99.996%!"],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/ExchangeSinkExecSerializationTests.java","id":36262,"created_at":"2025-01-07T14:17:54Z","original_position":53,"side":"LEFT","position":74,"submitted_on_commit":"611ccae740ee25c64bfab1ca6b263be30c7c329d","diff_hunk":"@@ -126,12 +129,13 @@ public void testDeeplyNestedFields() throws IOException {\n      * with a single root field that has many children, grandchildren etc.\n      */\n     public void testDeeplyNestedFieldsKeepOnlyOne() throws IOException {\n-        ByteSizeValue expected \u003d ByteSizeValue.ofBytes(9425804);","submitted_line":129},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The byte size values in test cases have been adjusted due to changes in serialization. Verify that these new sizes accurately reflect the actual serialized data size after removing `EsIndex` mapping serialization.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/ExchangeSinkExecSerializationTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan